/T (Flask \(Python\). Chosen for minimal boilerplate, a synchronous request model that is straightforward to reason about and explain, and a mature, small ecosystem \(flask-cors, cookie- based session, flasgger\) that covered every requirement without extra scaffolding. Flask also integrates cleanly with TensorFlow/OpenCV running in-process for the facial-expression model, since both are just Python libraries imported and called from a route handler.)
/E (Flask \(Python\). Chosen for minimal boilerplate, a synchronous request model that is straightforward to reason about and explain, and a mature, small ecosystem \(flask-cors, cookie- based session, flasgger\) that covered every requirement without extra scaffolding. Flask also integrates cleanly with TensorFlow/OpenCV running in-process for the facial-expression model, since both are just Python libraries imported and called from a route handler.)
