/T (Presentation layer \(Browser / Frontend\). Static HTML/CSS/JavaScript pages served by a lightweight file server during development. Responsible only for rendering UI and making fetch\(\) calls to the backend with credentials: 'include' so the session cookie travels with every request.)
/E (Presentation layer \(Browser / Frontend\). Static HTML/CSS/JavaScript pages served by a lightweight file server during development. Responsible only for rendering UI and making fetch\(\) calls to the backend with credentials: 'include' so the session cookie travels with every request.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
